# .shipgate-allow -- recorded exceptions to ship_gate.py rules.
#
# Format:  <path glob> :: <rule id> :: <reason>
#
# Every rule blocks by default. A line here waives ONE rule for ONE path glob,
# and the scan prints every exception it applies, so nothing is waived silently.
# Rule id "*" waives all rules for a path -- avoid it; it is flagged loudly.
#
# Only the repository maintainer adds lines here. Keep globs narrow and always
# say WHY: the reason is the audit trail for a future reader asking
# "was this actually checked?".

# --- contract registries: public infrastructure, not per-account data --------
# These list GoodDollar/Uniswap/Ubeswap contract addresses. Confirmed 2026-09-23
# that none of them contain user wallets.
docs/subgraph/*.txt :: content:address-list :: subgraph manifests, contract addresses and start blocks only
projects/onchain-analytics/contracts/ABIs/*.csv :: content:address-list :: contract ABI export, deployed contract addresses only
projects/onchain-analytics/contracts/README.md :: content:address-list :: the contract registry doc, by definition a list of contracts
queries/dune/reserve-analysis/lp-v3-positions.sql :: content:address-list :: Uniswap V3 pool contract addresses

# --- dbt seeds: address + number pairs, but the number is not a balance -------
projects/onchain-analytics/gd_dbt/seeds/contract_deployments.csv :: content:holder-table :: contract address paired with its deployment BLOCK, not a holder balance
projects/onchain-analytics/gd_dbt/seeds/tokens.csv :: content:holder-table :: token contract address paired with its DECIMALS, not a holder balance

# --- reader-facing docs that trip a filename or attribution rule -------------
projects/goodwidget-components/spec.md :: name:spec.md :: real component specification, reader-facing product doc, not a pipeline artifact
projects/goodbuilders-s4/README.md :: content:colleague-name :: repo ownership table; naming the owner of a public GoodDollar repo is the point of the column
